  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JSB2025_Northeast Reset Fostering Stabilisation and Resilience for Early Transition of Communities Affected by Extremist Violence and Climate Change in Northeast Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities in Borno State, Northeast Nigeria, continue to recover from the prolonged impacts of the Boko Haram insurgency, compounded by climate shocks and economic fragility. While stabilization interventions under the Regional Stabilization Facility (RSF) have improved security, restored basic services, and reactivated community structures, many households and local economies remain vulnerable due to limited livelihood opportunities, low productivity, and weak systems for sustaining community</narrative>
  </description>
